# What `git archive` leaves out — and so what Packagist's dist and GitHub's
# tag tarballs (the source vcpkg and Conan Center fetch) leave out.
#
# Only the user documentation ships. docs/ is an allowlist, as in package.json
# and pyproject.toml: everything under it is excluded, then the user documents
# are let back in, so a new interim note cannot reach a release by default.
# tools/check-package-docs.sh holds all three to the same list.
docs/**                  export-ignore
docs/README.md                -export-ignore
docs/overview.md              -export-ignore
docs/parity.md                -export-ignore
docs/syntax.md                -export-ignore
docs/operators.md             -export-ignore
docs/functions.md             -export-ignore
docs/sql.md                   -export-ignore
docs/extending.md             -export-ignore
# A directory matched by docs/** is dropped whole, so the two that hold user
# documents are let back in; their files are still allowlisted one by one.
docs/usage                    -export-ignore
docs/reference                -export-ignore
docs/usage/README.md          -export-ignore
docs/usage/repl.md            -export-ignore
docs/usage/validation.md      -export-ignore
docs/usage/scripting.md       -export-ignore
docs/usage/sql-conditions.md  -export-ignore
docs/usage/sql-pipelines.md   -export-ignore
docs/usage/sql-star.md        -export-ignore
docs/usage/sql-eav.md         -export-ignore
docs/usage/sql-3nf.md         -export-ignore
docs/usage/sql-flat.md        -export-ignore
docs/usage/in-memory.md       -export-ignore
docs/reference/builtins.md    -export-ignore
docs/reference/limits.md      -export-ignore

# Maintainer and agent instructions.
PACKAGING.md             export-ignore
CLAUDE.md                export-ignore
